{
  "_about": "Gym vocabulary for translating exercise names and instructions to Spanish. Edit freely: scripts/translate_catalog.py sends this to the model and uses the 'check' stems to verify every translation. 'es' is the preferred term; 'also' lists accepted alternatives; 'check' is a lowercase, accent-free stem that must appear in the Spanish name when the English term appears in the English name (omit it for terms that may be dropped or rephrased).",
  "style": [
    "Neutral Latin American Spanish that also reads naturally in Spain; informal 'tú'.",
    "Names: use the name Spanish-speaking gym-goers actually use, not a word-for-word translation. Keep established English terms (press, curl, crunch, hip thrust, burpee, swing, pullover) as-is.",
    "Name order: movement first, then equipment, then position/grip/variant. E.g. 'Dumbbell Incline Bench Press' -> 'Press de banca inclinado con mancuernas'.",
    "Plural equipment when the exercise uses two: 'con mancuernas'; singular when one-arm: 'con mancuerna a una mano'.",
    "Keep proper names as-is (Arnold, Zottman, Pallof, Smith, Scott, Bulgarian -> búlgara, Romanian -> rumano).",
    "Drop ExerciseDB tags that carry no meaning for users: 'v2', 'v3', 'pov', '(male)', '(female)'.",
    "Instructions: imperative 'tú' ('Acuéstate', 'Sujeta', 'Baja'), same number of steps as the English, no added advice, units and numbers unchanged."
  ],
